/-!
# Stacks 01HN: the closed subspace cut out by a locally generated ideal sheaf

Let `X` be a locally ringed space and let `j : J ⟶ 𝒪_X` be a sheaf of ideals, presented as a
monomorphism of sheaves of `𝒪_X`-modules into the structure sheaf, and assume `J` is locally
generated by sections. Then there is a locally ringed space `Z` whose underlying space is the
support of `𝒪_X / J`, whose inclusion `Z ⟶ X` is a closed immersion, and whose ideal sheaf is
canonically `J`.

That is Stacks Tag 01HN, and it is the repository's canonical development in
`Stacks.ClosedImmersion`: `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.exists_closedSubspaceData`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ClosedImmersion/ClosedSubspaceExistence.lean`), with the tag
attached to `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.closedSubspace` in that file. Those declarations, and the
lemmas the construction is assembled from, are re-exported here and nothing is redeclared.

## Main declarations

* `ClosedSubspaceData` records the closed subspace, its inclusion, and the canonical
  quotient-sheaf and ideal-sheaf identifications. Both identifications carry a compatibility
  equation pinning them to `j` and to `cokernel.π j`, so the quotient structure sheaf is
  identified canonically rather than merely up to an arbitrary isomorphism.
* `exists_closedSubspaceData` is the existence of the construction, and `closedSubspace` is a
  choice of it.
* `ideal_kernelLift_isIso` is the step identifying the ideal sheaf of the resulting inclusion
  with `J`: the canonical `kernel.lift` is a monomorphism because it factors `j`, which is one,
  and an epimorphism by local exactness of `𝒪_X ⟶ 𝒪_X / J` at `J`
  (`supportStructureMap_locally_exact`). The quotient identification is then forced: once `J`
  is the kernel of an epimorphism, that epimorphism is a cokernel of `j`.

## Implementation notes

These names were originally a second, content-identical copy of the canonical declarations,
whose supporting lemmas were `private` and so unreachable. The bodies agreed line for line but
the constants were distinct, so `Stacks.ClosedSubspaceIdeal.closedSubspace` carried its own
Tag 01HN attribute and was not interchangeable with the tagged canonical one. The supporting
lemmas are now public and this file aliases the canonical declarations, so the two spellings
are one constant and the tag is registered once.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01HN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01HN)
-/

